     1	"""Admin settings API router (public-multiuser-release Phase 5, P5.6 T2;
     2	extended Phase 3 (public-multiuser-release-activation), ACT-301..303).
     3	
     4	Exposes workspace-management, auth-provider status, rate-limit config,
     5	service-account + personal-access-token (PAT) management, and
     6	deployment-mode-status endpoints that the admin settings panel (P5.8)
     7	consumes.
     8	
     9	Role gating
    10	-----------
    11	Every route in this router except the two documented self-service exceptions
    12	below is gated with ``require_role("owner", "admin")`` from
    13	:mod:`~research_foundry.api.auth.rbac`. No other bespoke auth checks are used
    14	for those routes.
    15	
    16	Self-service exceptions (manual RBAC, NOT ``Depends(require_role(...))``):
    17	  * ``GET /api/admin/rbac-status`` — any authenticated user (pre-existing).
    18	  * ``POST/GET /api/admin/pats``, ``DELETE /api/admin/pats/{token_id}`` — any
    19	    authenticated user may self-issue/list/revoke their OWN PATs; acting on
    20	    another user's PAT requires owner/admin (403, not a 404-leak — see the
    21	    PAT section below). These routes are exempt from the blanket
    22	    ``require_role`` route-sweep check for the same documented reason
    23	    ``reports.py``'s ``publish-preview`` route is: the permission decision
    24	    depends on request BODY/PATH content (whose PAT), not just the caller's
    25	    role, so it cannot be expressed as a single static ``Depends(...)``.
    26	
    27	Endpoints
    28	---------
    29	GET   /api/admin/workspace                              — member list for caller's workspace
    30	PATCH /api/admin/members/{user_id}/role                  — update a member's role
    31	GET   /api/admin/auth-provider-status                    — active provider + availability
    32	GET   /api/admin/rate-limit-config                       — current rate-limit budget
    33	PATCH /api/admin/rate-limit-config                       — update rate-limit budget (in-memory)
    34	GET   /api/admin/rbac-status                              — RBAC enforcement state (any authed user)
    35	POST  /api/admin/service-accounts                         — create a service account
    36	GET   /api/admin/service-accounts                         — list service accounts (paginated)
    37	DELETE /api/admin/service-accounts/{id}                   — disable a service account
    38	POST  /api/admin/service-accounts/{id}/tokens             — issue/rotate its access token
    39	GET   /api/admin/service-accounts/{id}/tokens             — list its tokens (paginated, no secrets)
    40	DELETE /api/admin/service-accounts/{id}/tokens/{token_id} — revoke a specific token
    41	POST  /api/admin/pats                                      — issue a PAT (self, or on-behalf via owner/admin)
    42	GET   /api/admin/pats                                      — list PATs (self, or any via owner/admin)
    43	DELETE /api/admin/pats/{token_id}                          — revoke a PAT (self, or any via owner/admin)
    44	GET   /api/admin/deployment-mode-status                    — resolved deployment_mode + gate conditions
    45	
    46	Response contract (matches P5.8 frontend assumptions — do not change field names):
    47	
    48	GET /api/admin/workspace
    49	    { "workspace_id": str, "members": list[{user_id, email, role}] | null }
    50	
    51	PATCH /api/admin/members/{user_id}/role
    52	    body: { "role": str }  → 200 on success, 404 when member not found
    53	
    54	GET /api/admin/rate-limit-config
    55	    { "enabled": bool, "window_seconds": int, "max_requests": int,
    56	      "per_identity": true, "per_route": true }
    57	
    58	PATCH /api/admin/rate-limit-config
    59	    body: { "max_requests"?: int, "window_seconds"?: int }
    60	    → 200 with updated config on success
    61	    NOTE: ``enabled`` is a startup-only setting (foundry.yaml auth.rate_limit.enabled)
    62	    and cannot be toggled at runtime — include it in the body and it is silently ignored.
    63	
    64	GET /api/admin/auth-provider-status
    65	    { "provider": str, "available": bool, "details"?: str }
    66	    NOTE: NEVER returns raw keys, JWKS secrets, or Bearer tokens.
    67	
    68	GET /api/admin/rbac-status
    69	    { "rbac_enforcement": str, "rbac_enforced": bool, "auth_provider": str }
    70	
    71	Service accounts / PATs / tokens (Phase 3, ACT-301/ACT-302)
    72	-------------------------------------------------------------
    73	POST /api/admin/service-accounts
    74	    body: { "name": str, "role": str, "description"?: str }
    75	    → 201 { "id", "name", "workspace_id", "role", "description", "created_by",
    76	             "created_at", "disabled_at" } — NEVER a token/secret.
    77	
    78	GET /api/admin/service-accounts?limit=&offset=
    79	    → { "items": [...same shape as above...], "total": int, "limit": int, "offset": int }
    80	
    81	DELETE /api/admin/service-accounts/{id}
    82	    → { "id": str, "disabled": true } ; 404 if unknown or in another workspace.
    83	
    84	POST /api/admin/service-accounts/{id}/tokens
    85	    body: { "expires_at"?: str }
    86	    Issues a fresh token for the account, revoking any prior ACTIVE token for
    87	    it first (rotate-on-issue — never more than one live token per service
    88	    account). → 201 { "token_id", "plaintext", "token_prefix",
    89	    "principal_type", "principal_id", "workspace_id", "role", "expires_at" }
    90	    **``plaintext`` is shown here ONLY — never again, never logged.**
    91	
    92	GET /api/admin/service-accounts/{id}/tokens?limit=&offset=
    93	    → { "items": [{"token_id","token_prefix","created_at","expires_at",
    94	                    "revoked_at","last_used_at"}...], "total", "limit", "offset" }
    95	    NEVER includes ``token_hash`` or a plaintext secret.
    96	
    97	DELETE /api/admin/service-accounts/{id}/tokens/{token_id}
    98	    → { "token_id": str, "revoked": true } ; 404 if unknown / wrong account.
    99	
   100	POST /api/admin/pats
   101	    body: { "role": str, "expires_at"?: str, "user_id"?: str }
   102	    Self-issues a PAT for the caller by default. Setting ``user_id`` to
   103	    someone else requires the caller's role to include owner/admin (403
   104	    otherwise). → 201, same shape as the service-account token response.
   105	    **``plaintext`` is shown here ONLY.**
   106	
   107	GET /api/admin/pats?user_id=&limit=&offset=
   108	    Lists the caller's own PATs by default; ``user_id`` targeting another
   109	    user requires owner/admin (403, never a silent empty list).
   110	    → { "items": [...token metadata, no secrets...], "total", "limit", "offset" }
   111	
   112	DELETE /api/admin/pats/{token_id}
   113	    Revokes a PAT. Non-owner/admin callers may only revoke their OWN PAT —
   114	    a same-workspace PAT belonging to someone else yields 403 (existence is
