     1	"""Report claim verifier — the differentiated value of Research Foundry.
     2	
     3	``verify_report`` is the gate between "a model wrote some markdown" and "a report
     4	you can rely on". It deterministically enforces spec §12.3: every material claim
     5	in the report body must either carry a ``[claim:<id>]`` tag that resolves to the
     6	run's claim ledger, or be explicitly labeled as an inference/speculation. It also
     7	enforces ledger-side invariants (supported claims have source cards, inference
     8	claims have a basis) and governance (work-sensitive sources may not leak into a
     9	public report).
    10	
    11	The verifier never calls the network and never needs an API key. Exit codes
    12	follow the stable contract in :mod:`research_foundry.errors` with this
    13	precedence (first that applies wins):
    14	
    15	1. missing front matter / schema failure  -> ExitCode.SCHEMA (2)
    16	2. work-sensitive source in a public report -> ExitCode.GOVERNANCE (3)
    17	3. any unsupported material claim / unsupported ledger claim -> ExitCode.UNSUPPORTED (4)
    18	4. otherwise                                -> ExitCode.OK (0)
    19	"""
