     1	"""Access-token issuance, verification, and revocation (public-multiuser-release
     2	Phase 2, ACT-202).
     3	
     4	OQ-1 resolution: this module lives under ``services/`` as a peer of
     5	``rbac_store.py`` / ``audit_service.py`` — it is business logic (crypto,
     6	role-ceiling policy) layered on top of ``rbac_store``'s pure data-access
     7	helpers, not an ``api/auth`` adapter itself.  ``AuthProviderMiddleware``
     8	(``api/middleware/auth.py``, ACT-203) calls :func:`verify_token` directly; it
     9	is NOT registered in the ``AuthProvider`` registry (``api/auth/provider.py``)
    10	because token-store resolution runs *before* the provider-adapter chain, not
    11	as one more adapter in it.
    12	
    13	Security invariants (FR-7..FR-10)
    14	----------------------------------
    15	1. The plaintext secret is generated fresh per token via :mod:`secrets`
    16	   (CSPRNG, >= 256 bits) and returned to the caller **exactly once**, at
    17	   issuance (:class:`IssuedToken.plaintext`).  It is never stored, logged, or
    18	   echoed back by any other function in this module.
