    20	   short non-secret prefix are persisted, via ``rbac_store.create_access_token``.
    21	3. All verification comparisons use ``hmac.compare_digest`` — never ``==``.
    22	   A prefix miss still performs a same-shape dummy comparison so resolution
    23	   time does not depend on whether a candidate row was found (closes the
    24	   prefix-based timing side channel called out in ACT-203's acceptance
    25	   criteria).
    26	4. Revocation and expiry (FR-10) and the PAT role-ceiling (FR-9) are checked
    27	   fresh on every :func:`verify_token` call — never cached, never resolved
    28	   only at issuance.
    29	5. No function in this module ever raises on "no match" / "invalid" /
    30	   "expired" / "revoked" — :func:`verify_token` returns ``None`` uniformly
    31	   for all of those so the composite auth chain's fall-through-to-provider
    32	   behavior (AC-2, AC-4) never has to distinguish a genuine token-store
    33	   outage from an unrecognized token.
