   126	
   127	Both functions return the run dict and always write `search_run.yaml` (or the
   128	extraction equivalent) to disk before returning. Failures land in
   129	`run["schema_errors"]`, not in raised exceptions.
   130	
   131	---
   132	
   133	## 5. Running the Optional MCP Server
   134	
   135	Install `mcp` extra, then:
   136	
   137	```bash
   138	uv run python -m research_foundry.services.search_router.mcp_server
   139	```
   140	
   141	The module **imports cleanly without `mcp` installed**; only `build_server()`
   142	and `main()` try to resolve the SDK, and they raise a clear `RuntimeError`
   143	asking you to `uv sync --extra mcp` if it's missing.
   144	
   145	**Tool naming.** Tool names are the underscored Python function names the
   146	`@server.tool()` decorator derives by default — *not* a dotted form. This
   147	list must stay in sync with `mcp_server.py` (the module docstring there is
   148	the source of truth). Tools registered today:
   149	
   150	- `search_run` — wraps `run_search(request)`
   151	- `extract_url` — wraps `extract_urls(urls)`
   152	- `search_source_discovery` — mode-preset for `mode="source_discovery"` (Brave → Exa)
   153	- `search_semantic_discovery` — mode-preset for `mode="semantic_discovery"` (Exa → GitHub → Brave)
   154	- `search_github_discovery` — mode-preset for `mode="github_discovery"` (GitHub → Exa → Brave)
   155	- `search_quick_lookup` — mode-preset for `mode="quick_lookup"` (Brave; fast, low-cost)
   156	- `search_official_sources` — mode-preset for `mode="official_source_check"` (Brave → Exa; authoritative domains)
   157	- `search_academic_discovery` — mode-preset for `mode="academic_discovery"` (OpenAlex / Semantic Scholar / PubMed / arXiv)
   158	
   159	Every mode-preset tool is a thin shim that fills in `mode` on the request
   160	before delegating to `run_search` — no new business logic. This covers the
   161	minimum tool surface from spec §10.2 needed for an agent harness to drive the
   162	router. The full surface (`crawl.site`, `research.build_source_cards`,
   163	`research.verify_claims`, `research.monitor_query`, …) is deferred.
   164	
   165	### Registering with an MCP-aware harness
   166	
   167	A repo-root `.mcp.json` registers the server for Claude Code (and other
   168	MCP-aware harnesses) to auto-discover:
   169	
   170	```json
   171	{
   172	  "mcpServers": {
   173	    "rf-mcp": {
   174	      "type": "stdio",
   175	      "command": "python",
   176	      "args": ["-m", "research_foundry.services.search_router.mcp_server"],
   177	      "cwd": "${workspaceFolder}"
   178	    }
   179	  }
   180	}
   181	```
   182	
   183	Requires the `mcp` extra installed in whatever interpreter `command` resolves
   184	to (`uv sync --extra mcp`); if you've installed the console script via
   185	`uv tool install --editable .`, `command: "rf-mcp"` with no `args` works too.
   186	
   187	---
