   201	    # whatever foundry.yaml's `viewer.sensitivity_threshold` said instead
   202	    # (`"public"` in the shipped config).
   203	    #
   204	    # Storing the resolved value on app.state — the same pattern already used
   205	    # for rbac_enforced/workspace_isolation_enforced above — lets the catalog
   206	    # router pass it through as `resolve_threshold()`'s explicit `override`
   207	    # argument. When no CLI flag was passed, config.viewer.get(...) is
   208	    # whatever foundry.yaml already had, so this is a no-op relative to prior
   209	    # behavior — the fail-closed default (`"public"`) is unchanged.
   210	    #
   211	    # Resolution order (catalog_service.resolve_threshold): explicit `rf serve
   212	    # --sensitivity-threshold` > foundry.yaml viewer.sensitivity_threshold >
   213	    # hardcoded "public" default (the latter two remain resolve_threshold's
   214	    # own responsibility when this override is None).
   215	    app.state.catalog_sensitivity_threshold = config.viewer.get("sensitivity_threshold") or None
